  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Introducing Sustainable Agro-Eco-Technol</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to introduce and practice innovative, sustainable agro-eco-technologies in Qalqilya or Jenin Governorate, Palestine to enhance vocational education in the agricultural sector. The existing vocational education curricula and resources are limitedand require improvement to meet market needs and technological advancements. The project will establish two ecological agriculturaldemonstrations in two vocational schools and provide training to 30 students and 10 teachers on green and climate-resilient technologies in agriculture. The project will also enhance awareness and understanding of the new technologies among students&apos; families, communities, and farmers.

In collaboration with Oxfam, Arij will be the partner in this project. The project will provide benefits toteachers, students, student families, community and local farmers, and youth females and women. The long-term goal of the intervention is to raise awareness of sustainable agricultural practices, enhance the quality of vocational education in the agricultural sector, and promote a more sustainable and resilient agricultural industry in Qalqilya or Jenin, Palestine.</narrative>
  </description>
